---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
import '../styles/remodel.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="boomley — problems become signals" description="boomley is a two-person product company and growing community for turning meaningful problems into products worth building.">
  <div class="loader" data-loader aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="loader-count"><span data-loader-count>000</span>%</div>
    <div class="loader-copy" data-loader-copy>WE ALL HAVE THEM.</div>
    <div class="loader-logo" data-loader-logo>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="18" y="16" width="28" height="7" rx="1.5" class="signal-dash"/>
        <path d="M18 28h18c8 0 12 4 12 10s-4 10-12 10H18zm10 7v6h8c2 0 4-1 4-3s-2-3-4-3z"/>
      </svg>
      <span>boomley</span>
    </div>
    <div class="loader-welcome" data-loader-welcome>WELCOME.</div>
  </div>

  <header class="site-nav">
    <a href="#top" class="brand" aria-label="boomley home">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="18" y="16" width="28" height="7" rx="1.5" class="signal-dash"/>
        <path d="M18 28h18c8 0 12 4 12 10s-4 10-12 10H18zm10 7v6h8c2 0 4-1 4-3s-2-3-4-3z"/>
      </svg>
      <span>boomley</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#process">Process</a>
      <a href="#builds">Builds</a>
      <a href="#community">Community</a>
    </nav>
    <a class="signal-cta" href="#signal-box">Send a signal ↗</a>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A PRODUCT COMPANY / A PUBLIC WORKBENCH / A GROWING COMMUNITY</p>
        <h1>
          Problems are
          <span>everywhere.</span>
          We pay attention.
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-deck">boomley notices the problems people keep learning to live with — then investigates the ones worth turning into products.</p>
        <div class="hero-meta">
          <span>02 PEOPLE</span>
          <span>01 ACTIVE BUILD</span>
          <span>EST. 2026</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-visual" data-founder-rotator>
        <article class="founder-tile" data-founder-tile="chidi">
          <img src="/media/founders/chidi.webp" width="2048" height="2048" alt="Chidi, Product" />
          <span>PRODUCT</span>
        </article>
        <article class="founder-tile" data-founder-tile="michael">
          <img src="/media/founders/michael.webp" width="2048" height="2048" alt="Michael, Engineering" />
          <span>ENGINEERING</span>
        </article>
        <div class="hero-sticker">TWO PEOPLE.<br/>FOR NOW.</div>
        <div class="hero-signal-card">
          <span>SIGNAL RECEIVER</span>
          <b>01</b>
          <i></i>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-scroll">SCROLL TO TRACE THE SIGNAL ↓</div>
    </section>

    <section class="signal-strip" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>PROBLEM</span><b>→</b><span>THOUGHT</span><b>→</b><span>IDEA</span><b>→</b><span>SIGNAL</span><b>→</b><span>boomley</span>
    </section>

    <section id="about" class="about">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span>01 / ABOUT</span>
        <p>We don't start with apps. We start by asking whether the problem deserves one.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-copy">
          <h2>It starts with a <em>problem.</em></h2>
          <p>Something takes too long. Feels unnecessarily difficult. Makes people invent workarounds.</p>

          <h2>Then a <em>thought.</em></h2>
          <p>Why does it work this way? Why has everybody accepted it?</p>

          <h2>Then an <em>idea.</em></h2>
          <p>Not necessarily a product yet. Just the possibility that something could be better.</p>

          <h2>Then a <em>signal.</em></h2>
          <p>When the pattern repeats, boomley starts listening more closely.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="signal-lab">
          <div class="signal-lab-top"><span>LIVE SIGNAL INTERPRETATION</span><span>001</span></div>
          <pre class="ascii-field" data-ascii-field aria-hidden="true">....::::;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@
...::::;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@@
..::::;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@@@
.::::;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@@@@
::::;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@@@@@
:::;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@@@@@@
::;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@@@@@@@
:;;;;iiiirrrrssssXXXXAAAA2533hhMMHHGGSS##9B&@@@@@@@@</pre>
          <div class="signal-lab-center">
            <div class="scan-ring" data-scan-ring><span>SEARCHING</span></div>
            <p>Noise is everywhere.<br/>The pattern is the interesting part.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="signal-lab-bottom"><span>PROBLEM → THOUGHT → IDEA</span><b>SIGNAL</b></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="process" class="process">
      <div class="process-sticky">
        <div class="section-head section-head--dark">
          <span>02 / HOW WE WORK</span>
          <p>One continuous loop. No theatre.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-layout">
          <div class="process-copy">
            <h2>We don't start<br/>with <span>apps.</span></h2>
            <p>We start by asking whether the problem deserves one.</p>
            <div class="process-tabs" role="list">
              <button class="is-active" data-process-tab="0">01 NOTICE</button>
              <button data-process-tab="1">02 LISTEN</button>
              <button data-process-tab="2">03 QUESTION</button>
              <button data-process-tab="3">04 BUILD</button>
              <button data-process-tab="4">05 TEST</button>
              <button data-process-tab="5">06 LISTEN AGAIN</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="process-stage" data-process-stage>
            <div class="process-orbit" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <article class="process-card is-active">
              <span>01 / NOTICE</span>
              <h3>Find repeated friction rather than isolated annoyance.</h3>
              <div class="process-graphic graphic-noise"></div>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>02 / LISTEN</span>
              <h3>Understand who experiences it and what it costs them.</h3>
              <div class="process-graphic graphic-wave"></div>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>03 / QUESTION</span>
              <h3>Decide whether software should exist at all.</h3>
              <div class="process-graphic graphic-grid"></div>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>04 / BUILD</span>
              <h3>Product and engineering turn the strongest signal into something tangible.</h3>
              <div class="process-graphic graphic-build"></div>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>05 / TEST</span>
              <h3>Reality gets the final vote.</h3>
              <div class="process-graphic graphic-test"></div>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>06 / LISTEN AGAIN</span>
              <h3>The loop starts over.</h3>
              <div class="process-graphic graphic-loop"></div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="history">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span>03 / HISTORY</span>
        <p>No mythology. No fake milestones. Just the actual beginning.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="history-intro">
        <h2>You found us <span>early.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="history-row">
        <article><span>2026</span><h3>Two disciplines meet.</h3><p>Product management and software engineering begin exploring recurring frustrations together.</p></article>
        <article><span>SIGNAL / 001</span><h3>Research begins.</h3><p>The first problem becomes serious enough to document rather than just discuss.</p></article>
        <article class="is-now"><span>NOW</span><h3>Building in public.</h3><p>Research, systems, experience design and the first private build are taking shape.</p></article>
        <article><span>NEXT</span><h3>Test with people.</h3><p>Let real users challenge the assumptions before anything deserves a launch.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="people" id="people">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span>04 / PEOPLE</span>
        <p>Two people. Two disciplines. One shared intolerance for unnecessary friction.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="people-title">
        <h2>Who's actually<br/>opening the box?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="people-grid" data-people-rotator>
        <article class="person" data-person="chidi">
          <div class="person-media">
            <img src="/media/founders/chidi.webp" width="2048" height="2048" alt="Chidi" />
            <canvas data-founder-ascii="chidi" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
            <div class="person-label"><span>PRODUCT</span><b>ASKS WHY.</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="person-meta"><b>CHIDI</b><span>Product management / strategy / research / experience</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="person" data-person="michael">
          <div class="person-media">
            <img src="/media/founders/michael.webp" width="2048" height="2048" alt="Michael" />
            <canvas data-founder-ascii="michael" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
            <div class="person-label"><span>ENGINEERING</span><b>MAKES IT REAL.</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="person-meta"><b>MICHAEL</b><span>Software engineering / systems / architecture / build</span></div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="people-note">Hover a portrait. The machine interprets the human.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="builds" class="builds">
      <div class="builds-intro">
        <span>05 / BUILDS</span>
        <p>WE FOUND OUR FIRST SIGNAL.</p>
        <h2>1000001</h2>
        <p class="builds-deck">We're not explaining it yet. We're documenting it, questioning it and building it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="builds-wall">
        <article class="artifact artifact--research">
          <span>RESEARCH / 001</span>
          <h3>ATTENTION WAS FRAGMENTED BEFORE WE TRIED TO FIX IT.</h3>
          <p>Research artifact / selected note</p>
        </article>

        <article class="artifact artifact--screen">
          <div class="browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>private build</span></div>
          <div class="mock-ui">
            <span>1000001 / INTERNAL</span>
            <h3>ONE THING.<br/>STAY WITH IT.</h3>
            <div class="mock-controls"><b></b><b></b><b></b></div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="artifact artifact--rule">
          <span>RULE / 07</span>
          <h3>THE TOOL SHOULD NOT BECOME THE TASK.</h3>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="status-rail">
        <div><span>RESEARCH</span><b>COMPLETE</b></div>
        <div><span>DOCUMENTATION</span><b>ACTIVE</b></div>
        <div><span>EXPERIENCE</span><b>ACTIVE</b></div>
        <div><span>BUILD</span><b>NEXT</b></div>
        <div><span>TEST</span><b>LATER</b></div>
      </div>

      <form class="waitlist" name="product-1000001" method="POST" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
        <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="product-1000001" />
        <p class="honeypot"><label>Do not fill this out: <input name="bot-field" /></label></p>
        <label for="product-email">Want to be there when 1000001 opens?</label>
        <div><input id="product-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="ENTER EMAIL" required autocomplete="email" /><button type="submit">KEEP ME CLOSE ↗</button></div>
        <p class="form-status" data-product-status aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section id="community" class="community">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span>06 / COMMUNITY</span>
        <p>boomley is becoming a home for problem-noticers, developers, designers, researchers, students, founders and people who are simply curious enough to ask why something still works this way.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="community-copy">
        <h2>Some people <span>notice things.</span></h2>
        <h2>Some people <span>build them.</span></h2>
        <p>We want both.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="community-grid" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="community-card card-a"><span>PROBLEM</span><b>?</b></div>
        <div class="community-card card-b"><pre>00101
11010
01011
10100</pre></div>
        <div class="community-card card-c"><span>BUILDERS</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <div class="community-card card-d"><span>SIGNAL</span><b>↗</b></div>
        <div class="community-card card-e"><span>WHY?</span><b>WHY?</b><strong>WHY?</strong></div>
        <div class="community-card card-f"><span>LISTEN</span><div class="wave"></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="community-actions">
        <a href="#signal-box">I HAVE A PROBLEM →</a>
        <a href="mailto:hello@boomley.com">I WANT TO BUILD →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="signal-box" class="signal-box">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span>07 / SEND A SIGNAL</span>
        <p>Don't pitch us an app. Tell us what shouldn't still be this difficult.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="signal-box-intro">
        <h2>What have <span>you</span> noticed?</h2>
        <div class="steps"><b><i>01</i> WRITE THE PROBLEM.</b><b><i>02</i> WRAP THE LETTER.</b><b><i>03</i> POST IT.</b></div>
      </div>

      <div class="signal-workspace">
        <form class="signal-form" name="boomley-signal" method="POST" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field" data-signal-form>
          <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="boomley-signal" />
          <p class="honeypot"><label>Do not fill this out: <input name="bot-field" /></label></p>
          <div class="letter-head"><span>boomley / signal form</span><span>001</span></div>
          <h3>WHAT'S BOTHERING YOU?</h3>
          <p>Write the problem. We'll worry about the product.</p>
          <label>THE PROBLEM<textarea name="friction" rows="4" required placeholder="It shouldn't still be this difficult to..."></textarea></label>
          <label>WHO DEALS WITH IT?<input name="who" type="text" required placeholder="People who..." /></label>
          <label>WHAT CHANGES IF IT'S FIXED?<textarea name="change" rows="2" required placeholder="It would make it easier to..."></textarea></label>
          <label>YOUR EMAIL<input name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" /></label>
          <div class="signal-actions"><button type="button" data-wrap>WRAP IT →</button><button type="submit" data-post disabled>POST IT →</button></div>
          <p class="form-status" data-signal-status aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>

        <div class="post-stage">
          <div class="envelope" data-envelope aria-hidden="true"><div class="paper">SIGNAL / READY</div><div class="flap"></div><span>TO / boomley</span></div>
          <div class="postbox" data-postbox>
            <div class="postbox-cap"></div>
            <div class="postbox-body">
              <div class="postbox-badge">b</div>
              <div class="postbox-slot"><span>POST SIGNAL</span></div>
              <div class="postbox-plaque"><b>boomley</b><small>SIGNAL RECEIVER / 001</small></div>
              <div class="postbox-door"><span>THE BOX IS OPEN</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="postbox-base"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ending">
      <canvas data-ending-field aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <div class="ending-copy">
        <span>SIGNALS EXIST EVERYWHERE.</span>
        <h2>This is only<br/><em>the beginning.</em></h2>
        <p>We're listening.</p>
        <div class="ending-brand">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="18" y="16" width="28" height="7" rx="1.5" class="signal-dash"/><path d="M18 28h18c8 0 12 4 12 10s-4 10-12 10H18zm10 7v6h8c2 0 4-1 4-3s-2-3-4-3z"/></svg>
          <b>boomley</b>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="footer-brand"><b>boomley</b><p>Problems become signals. Signals become things.</p></div>
    <div><span>EXPLORE</span><a href="#about">About</a><a href="#process">Process</a><a href="#builds">Builds</a><a href="#community">Community</a></div>
    <div><span>PARTICIPATE</span><a href="#signal-box">Send a Signal</a><a href="mailto:hello@boomley.com">Contact</a></div>
    <div><span>LEGAL</span><a href="#">Privacy</a><a href="#">Terms</a><small>© 2026 boomley</small></div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/remodel.ts';
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
